  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through Friday)\nIssued at 145 PM CDT SAT AUG 8 2026\n\nScattered afternoon showers and thunderstorms will remain in the\nforecast through the weekend, as this typical summertime pattern\nis expected to continue. PWAT values remain quite high, so\nlocally heavy rainfall is expected with slow storm motions. The\nupper-level pattern will slowly begin to break down by Monday, as\nthe ridge to our east starts to become more suppressed by the\ntrough to its north. At this time, the ridge appears to slide\nwest, reestablishing itself along the Gulf coast, remaining over\nthe Gulf Coast through Wednesday. It will begin to break down\nonce more by Thursday, as the trough to our north drops south\nonce again. Generally, this will keep rain in the forecast, but\nlimit it to the diurnally driven afternoon activity. More\norganized rain activity is possible as the trough drops south\nnext week, but confidence here is low since the best rain chances\nwould be tied to the location of the trough.\n\nAfternoon high temperatures will continue to run in the low to\nmid-90s, with the overall moisture content in the atmosphere\nremaining high. Because of that, afternoon heat index values will\ncontinue to reach triple-digits, but below heat headline criteria\nat this time.\n\n/44/",
